The visual QA system (internal/visualqa) returns findings with categories like text_overflow, contrast, spacing, alignment, font_size. The repair_slide tool accepts fix kinds like reduce_cell_text, replace_color, reshape_grid, swap_layout. There is ZERO translation layer between these two vocabularies. An agent that runs visual QA cannot automatically invoke repair_slide because it must manually interpret each finding category into a fix kind.

SCOPE:
1. Add SuggestedFixKind string and FixParams map[string]any fields to visualqa.Finding (internal/visualqa/types.go)
2. Create visualqa/repair_map.go with CategoryToFixKind mapping:
   - text_overflow → {"reduce_cell_text", "split_at_row", "reshape_grid"}
   - contrast → {"replace_color", "use_semantic_color"}
   - alignment → {"reshape_grid", "swap_layout"}
   - spacing → {"reshape_grid"}
   - font_size → {"reduce_text", "reshape_grid"}
   - missing_content → {"provide_value"}
3. In visualqa.parseFindings, populate SuggestedFixKind from the mapping
4. Add repair_slide kind "autofix_visual" that accepts a visual_qa_finding parameter and applies the mapped heuristic fix
5. Update loop_driver.go to use visual QA findings as a repair round before forcing split

ROOT CAUSE: session-history.md shows visual QA was never used because findings required manual interpretation. With this mapping, the repair loop can become fully autonomous.

ACCEPTANCE:
- visualqa.InspectSlide returns findings with suggested_fix_kind populated
- repair_slide accepts "autofix_visual" kind
- Loop driver can escalate to visual QA before forcing split
- End-to-end test: dense table → fit overflow → repair attempts → visual QA → autofix → pass

