## Expected Behavior

- Expose the existing native builders, which already accept bounds and shape-ID bases, through one shared bounded adapter used by placeholder and grid/compose dispatch; avoid separate duplicate implementations.
- Cover the ten canonical native types and three panel aliases in a data-driven short-fixture placement matrix. Preserve labels, values, editability, unique IDs, descriptions, theme and font behavior.
- At actual region dimensions, render when readable and otherwise return a precise capacity finding. Dense BMC/heatmap/framework content may correctly refuse half-width placement; do not force all types into narrow slots.
- Verify the PESTEL-plus-commentary reproduction at a viable size and a correctly refused dense variant, inspecting two templates. Keep unsupported placements unadvertised until implementation and render checks pass.

